.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt MK-WEB-MANIFEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk-web-manifest.sh
.Nd generate and verify a signed, RFC 3161 timestamped SHA-256 asset manifest
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl aLq
.Op Fl C Ar ca-file
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Op Fl k Ar gpg-key
.Op Fl m Ar manifest
.Op Fl t Ar tsa
.Op Fl x Ar pattern
.Op Fl -archive-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -ca-path Ar dir
.Op Fl -clearsign
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -gpg-homedir Ar dir
.Op Fl -include-vcs
.Op Fl -keep-tsq | Fl -no-keep-tsq
.Op Fl -timeout Ar seconds
.Op Fl -untrusted Ar cert-file
.Op Ar target-dir
.Nm
.Fl V
.Op Fl Lq
.Op Fl C Ar ca-file
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Op Fl m Ar manifest
.Op Fl x Ar pattern
.Op Fl -allow-untracked
.Op Fl -ca-path Ar dir
.Op Fl -gpg-homedir Ar dir
.Op Fl -include-vcs
.Op Fl -keyring Ar file
.Op Fl -no-ts-cert-verify
.Op Fl -untrusted Ar cert-file
.Op Ar target-dir
.Nm
.Fl P Ar file
.Op Fl Lq
.Op Fl C Ar ca-file
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Op Fl m Ar manifest
.Op Fl -archive-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -ca-path Ar dir
.Op Fl -gpg-homedir Ar dir
.Op Fl -keyring Ar file
.Op Fl -no-ts-cert-verify
.Op Fl -untrusted Ar cert-file
.Op Ar target-dir
.Nm
.Fl -list-tsa
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates and verifies a cryptographic attestation bundle for static web
assets or release directories using strictly POSIX-compliant shell facilities.
.Pp
In generation mode (the default),
.Nm
performs four atomic steps inside a private staging directory before committing
the resulting artifacts to
.Ar target-dir
(which defaults to the current working directory):
.Bl -enum
.It
Scans
.Ar target-dir
for regular files, rejects paths containing control characters, backslashes, or
unexpected symbolic links, and produces a locale-independent, deterministically
sorted
.Pa SHA256SUMS
manifest.
.It
Signs the manifest using GnuPG with SHA-256, producing a detached ASCII-armored
signature
.Pq Pa SHA256SUMS.asc
and immediately self-verifying the signature.
.It
Generates an RFC 3161 TimeStampReq query
.Pq Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsq
containing a SHA-256 message imprint of the signature file and a random
64-bit cryptographic nonce.
.It
Submits the query via HTTPS/HTTP to a configurable RFC 3161 Time Stamping
Authority (TSA), validates the returned TimeStampResp DER token
.Pq Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsr
for a
.Dq Granted
status, matching SHA-256 message imprint, and matching cryptographic nonce, and
atomically moves all verified artifacts into
.Ar target-dir .
.El
.Pp
In verification mode
.Pq Fl V / Fl -verify ,
.Nm
performs three-layer cryptographic verification in strict outer-to-inner order:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Sy Temporal Proof (RFC 3161 Timestamp) :
Validates the DER structure, status, SHA-256 message imprint, nonce, and X.509
certificate trust chain of
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsr
(and
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsq
if present) against
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc .
.It
.Sy Authenticity (GPG Signature) :
Verifies the GnuPG signature in
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc
against
.Pa SHA256SUMS ,
requiring explicit
.Dv GOODSIG
and
.Dv VALIDSIG
status tokens and rejecting weak digest algorithms (MD5, SHA-1, RIPEMD-160).
.It
.Sy Asset Integrity (SHA-256 Checksums & Directory Bijection) :
Validates the manifest against path traversal, duplicate entries, and control
characters, verifies every listed file's SHA-256 digest on disk, and ensures no
untracked files exist in
.Ar target-dir .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl V , Fl -verify
Verify existing attestation artifacts in
.Ar target-dir
instead of generating new ones.
.It Fl P Ar file , Fl -prove Ar file
Prove the earliest publication timestamp of
.Ar file
by scanning both archived proof bundles in
.Pa proofs/
(or
.Fl -archive-dir )
and the active root manifest, cryptographically verifying each matching
bundle's RFC 3161 timestamp and GnuPG signature against the file's current
SHA-256 digest.
.It Fl a , Fl -archive
When regenerating a manifest in a directory that already has an attestation
bundle, compare current asset hashes against the existing manifest.
If no tracked files have changed (and
.Fl -force
is not given), exit 0 without re-signing or replacing the existing RFC 3161
timestamp.
If files have changed, rotate the previous attestation bundle into
.Pa proofs/<ISO-timestamp>/
(and chain its hashes into the new root manifest) so original publication date
proofs for unchanged files are permanently preserved.
.It Fl -archive-dir Ar dir
Use
.Ar dir
(relative to
.Ar target-dir ,
default:
.Pa proofs )
for storing and searching archived proof bundles.
Implies
.Fl a .
.It Fl -force
Force manifest regeneration (and archiving of the previous bundle when
.Fl a
is active) even if no tracked asset hashes have changed.
.It Fl d Ar dir , Fl -dir Ar dir
Operate on directory
.Ar dir .
May also be specified as the positional
.Ar target-dir
argument.
.It Fl m Ar name , Fl -manifest Ar name
Use
.Ar name
as the manifest filename instead of the default
.Pa SHA256SUMS .
Must be a simple filename without path separators or leading dots.
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -gpg-key Ar key
Sign the manifest using the specified GnuPG key ID, fingerprint, or user ID.
.It Fl -gpg-homedir Ar dir
Use
.Ar dir
as the GnuPG home directory
.Pq Ql gpg --homedir .
.It Fl -keyring Ar file
Use an additional GnuPG keyring file during signature verification.
.It Fl -clearsign
Generate an inline clearsigned signature instead of a detached ASCII-armored
signature.
.It Fl t Ar tsa , Fl -tsa Ar tsa
Select the RFC 3161 Time Stamping Authority by preset name (see
.Sx TSA PRESETS )
or by full
.Ql https://
or
.Ql http://
endpoint URL.
Defaults to
.Cm freetsa .
.It Fl -list-tsa
Display the table of built-in RFC 3161 TSA presets and exit.
.It Fl -timeout Ar seconds
Maximum time in seconds allowed for the TSA network request.
Defaults to 30.
.It Fl -keep-tsq
Retain the
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsq
query artifact alongside
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsr
after generation (default).
.It Fl -no-keep-tsq
Delete the
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsq
query artifact after generation.
.It Fl C Ar file , Fl -ca-file Ar file
Trusted CA certificate bundle in PEM format for X.509 verification of the TSA
response token
.Pq Ql openssl ts -verify -CAfile .
.It Fl -ca-path Ar dir
Directory of hashed trusted CA certificates for TSA verification
.Pq Ql openssl ts -verify -CApath .
.It Fl -untrusted Ar file
Additional untrusted intermediate certificates in PEM format for TSA
verification
.Pq Ql openssl ts -verify -untrusted .
.It Fl -no-ts-cert-verify
During
.Fl V / Fl -verify ,
verify the RFC 3161 token structure, status, SHA-256 message imprint, and nonce,
but skip X.509 CA root trust chain validation.
.It Fl x Ar pattern , Fl -exclude Ar pattern
Exclude files or directories matching the glob
.Ar pattern .
May be specified multiple times.
.It Fl -include-vcs
Do not automatically exclude
.Pa .git ,
.Pa .hg ,
and
.Pa .svn
version control directories.
.It Fl L , Fl -follow-symlinks
Follow symbolic links when scanning and verifying files.
By default, symbolic links are rejected for security.
.It Fl -allow-untracked
During
.Fl V / Fl -verify ,
emit a warning instead of failing when untracked files are found in
.Ar target-dir .
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Suppress informational progress messages; only warnings and errors are written
to standard error.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display usage information and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Display version string and exit.
.El
.Sh TSA PRESETS
The following preset names may be passed to
.Fl t / Fl -tsa
or set in
.Ev TSA_URL :
.Bl -tag -width "globalsign"
.It Cm freetsa
.Lk https://freetsa.org/tsr
(default)
.It Cm digicert
.Lk https://timestamp.digicert.com
.It Cm sectigo
.Lk https://timestamp.sectigo.com
.It Cm globalsign
.Lk http://timestamp.globalsign.com/tsa/r6advanced1
.It Cm entrust
.Lk http://timestamp.entrust.net/TSS/RFC3161sha2TS
.It Cm apple
.Lk http://timestamp.apple.com/ts01
.It Cm identrust
.Lk http://timestamp.identrust.com
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "POSIX_MANIFEST_SHA256_BACKEND"
.It Ev TSA_URL
Default TSA preset name or endpoint URL (overridden by
.Fl t ) .
.It Ev GPG_KEY
Default GnuPG key ID or fingerprint for signing (overridden by
.Fl k ) .
.It Ev GPG_HOMEDIR
Default GnuPG home directory (overridden by
.Fl -gpg-homedir ) .
.It Ev GPG_KEYRING
Default GnuPG keyring file for verification (overridden by
.Fl -keyring ) .
.It Ev TSA_CA_FILE
Default trusted CA PEM file for RFC 3161 verification (overridden by
.Fl C ) .
.It Ev TSA_CA_PATH
Default trusted CA directory for RFC 3161 verification (overridden by
.Fl -ca-path ) .
.It Ev TSA_UNTRUSTED_FILE
Default untrusted intermediate certificate file (overridden by
.Fl -untrusted ) .
.It Ev TSA_TIMEOUT
Default HTTP request timeout in seconds (overridden by
.Fl -timeout ) .
.It Ev MANIFEST_NAME
Default manifest filename (overridden by
.Fl m ) .
.It Ev ARCHIVE_DIR
Default relative subdirectory for archived proof bundles (default:
.Pa proofs ;
overridden by
.Fl -archive-dir ) .
.It Ev KEEP_TSQ
Set to
.Ql 1
(default) to retain the
.Pa .tsq
query file or
.Ql 0
to remove it.
.It Ev POSIX_MANIFEST_SHA256_BACKEND
Optional override for the SHA-256 utility backend:
.Cm sha256sum ,
.Cm shasum ,
.Cm sha256 ,
or
.Cm openssl .
.It Ev TMPDIR
Directory in which the private
.Pq Li 0700
staging directory is created.
Defaults to
.Pa /tmp .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "SHA256SUMS.asc.tsr"
.It Pa SHA256SUMS
Deterministic, lexicographically sorted SHA-256 checksum manifest.
.It Pa SHA256SUMS.asc
ASCII-armored GnuPG signature over
.Pa SHA256SUMS .
.It Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsq
ASN.1 DER-encoded RFC 3161 TimeStampReq query for
.Pa SHA256SUMS.asc .
.It Pa SHA256SUMS.asc.tsr
ASN.1 DER-encoded RFC 3161 TimeStampResp token issued by the TSA.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv 0
Success.
.It Dv 1
General runtime or filesystem error.
.It Dv 2
Invalid command-line option, argument, or configuration.
.It Dv 3
Missing required external dependency
.Pq Xr gpg 1 , Xr openssl 1 , Xr curl 1 , or SHA-256 tool .
.It Dv 4
Manifest or asset integrity error (empty directory, unsafe filename, symbolic
link, path traversal, duplicate entry, checksum mismatch, or untracked file).
.It Dv 5
GnuPG signing or signature verification failure.
.It Dv 6
RFC 3161 timestamp query creation, TSA network request, or token verification
failure.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate an attestation bundle in
.Pa ./public
using the DigiCert TSA and a specific GPG signing key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mk-web-manifest.sh -t digicert -k 0xDEADBEEF12345678 ./public
.Ed
.Pp
Verify the attestation bundle in
.Pa ./public
using a custom TSA root CA certificate:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mk-web-manifest.sh -V -C /path/to/tsa-root-ca.pem ./public
.Ed
.Pp
Exclude source maps and temporary files during generation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mk-web-manifest.sh -x '*.map' -x '*.tmp' ./dist
.Ed
.Pp
Update a site while archiving previous proof bundles when files change (and
skipping if nothing changed):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mk-web-manifest.sh -a -t digicert ./site
.Ed
.Pp
Prove the earliest verified publication date of a specific file across archived
and active manifests:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mk-web-manifest.sh -P articles/whitepaper.pdf ./site
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr gpg 1 ,
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr sha256sum 1 ,
.Xr shasum 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
script conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008
(and IEEE Std 1003.1-2017 / 1003.1-2024).
Timestamp queries and responses conform to IETF RFC 3161 and RFC 5816.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Sy Atomic Staging :
All artifacts are constructed and self-verified in a mode
.Li 0700
temporary directory before being moved into
.Ar target-dir ,
preventing partial or unverified outputs from overwriting valid attestations on
failure.
.It
.Sy Path Traversal & Injection Prevention :
Filenames containing ASCII control characters (including newlines, carriage
returns, and ANSI terminal escape sequences) or backslashes are rejected during
both generation and verification.
During verification, parent directory traversal segments
.Pq Pa .. ,
absolute paths, symbolic links (unless
.Fl L
is specified), and duplicate manifest entries are strictly rejected.
.It
.Sy Verify-Then-Parse :
In verification mode, the RFC 3161 timestamp and GnuPG signature are verified
before manifest file paths are parsed or accessed.
.El
